  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **Edge picks reach the Boundary group in any pick mode** (`crates/ui/src/feature_click.rs`). An armed boundary row took the toolbar's pick kinds, so in Faces mode (the usual one) a click on an edge picked the face, and no edge could bound the cut. It now takes faces and edges whatever the mode. Points stay refused by name, as before.\n- **Two or more separate edges bound the area between them** (`crates/app/src/operation/boundary_chains.rs`, new; one arm in `boundary::resolve`). The open boundary may hold separate open chains. Each chain splits the stock the way a single chain does (`sides_of_chain`). Each keeps the side that holds the operation's own area, and the area kept is the area between the chains. A face bounded by two of its edges is faced between them, and the rows run on past the face at the open ends. Face lays its rows along the first chain. Side B keeps everything beyond the chains.\n- **Refused by name, never guessed** (each pinned and mutation-checked, below):\n  - chains that touch or cross (\"chains i and j touch or cross\");\n  - a chain with the operation's area evenly on both sides;\n  - a Contour given two chains (\"a Contour rides one open chain\");\n  - an include / exclude made of separate chains: the Apply door, as for one open chain (`PickShape::is_open` covers the new `PickShape::Chains`).\n- The old refusal \"the boundary picks spell N separate open runs\" is gone. The maintainer asked for exactly that case to work. The `area_picks.rs` assertion that pinned it now pins two chains.\n- Everything is a command: the picks go into the page draft, and Apply commits them as the existing undoable `EditOperationParams::with_area`. Over MCP, `set_operation_area`'s `open.picks` takes edge chain ids. It already accepted them; a test now pins it. The issue names `set_operation_geometry`, but that tool sets the operation's source and not its boundary. The decision file records this.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1727-boundary-edges.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- UI: `egui_app::tests::edge_click_modifiers::an_armed_boundary_row_takes_edges_in_faces_mode`. In Faces mode, with the row armed, a viewport click on an edge takes the edge, and a Ctrl+click adds a second separate edge (\"2 open chains\"). Apply commits both edges, and undo takes them back out.\n- Toolpath: `area_chains::a_face_bounded_by_two_of_its_edges_is_faced_between_them`. Face on the block's top with its north and south rim edges as the boundary: every feed has its tool edge within y +-20, works up to both edges, and runs past the face at both open ends. The verify is silent (0 warnings).\n- Refusals: `area_chains::chains_that_cross_are_refused_by_name`, `area_chains::a_contour_cannot_ride_two_separate_chains`, `area_chains::an_include_of_two_separate_chains_is_refused_at_apply` (this one also checks one undoable edit and its undo), `operation::boundary_chains::tests::the_area_lies_between_the_chains_and_a_tie_is_refused`, `operation::boundary_chains::tests::runs_group_into_chains_and_touching_chains_are_refused`.\n- MCP: `mcp_pick::edges_set_as_the_open_boundary_ride_one_undo_step`.\n\nMutation check: each refusal line was deleted (or neutralised), the named test was confirmed red, then the line was restored, the file touched, and `cmp` run against a backup:\n- touch check in `touching_refusal`: `chains_that_cross_are_refused_by_name` red;\n- its call site in `picks_geom`: `chains_that_cross_are_refused_by_name` red;\n- the tie check in `sides_of_chains`: `the_area_lies_between_the_chains_and_a_tie_is_refused` red;\n- the Contour arm in `contour_open::open_run`: `a_contour_cannot_ride_two_separate_chains` red;\n- `PickShape::Chains` in `is_open` (the Apply door): `an_include_of_two_separate_chains_is_refused_at_apply` red;\n- the UI pick-kinds fix itself: `an_armed_boundary_row_takes_edges_in_faces_mode` red.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --dry-run` selects nearly every app suite, because the gate map names `app::operation`. Under the budget I ran the targeted suites by name instead, all green on Linux:\n- app: `--lib`, `area_chains`, `area_controls`, `area_open`, `area_overhead`, `area_picks`, `stitch_cross`, `mcp_pick`;\n- ui: `--lib` (778 passed), `boundary`, `boundary_picks`, `edge_loop_pick`, `operations`, `feedback`;\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The other quick-plan app suites (not run, see above), the batch tier, the snapshots, and Windows.\n- The viewport's boundary overlay does not draw separate chains. The page lists the entry as \"N edges, M open chains\".\n- Side B (beyond the chains) for Face over a region in two pieces: Face's band check may refuse it by name. No test covers it.\n- Issue #1726 (open ends that extend for the 2D clearing kinds and do not turn the corner) is a separate `effort:max` law. This PR does not do it, although it uses the same chain grouping.\n\nBranched from upstream/main 0db66c44, which none of the open Geometry-tab PRs (#1701, #1710, #1711) collide with: this PR does not touch `geo_page.rs`.\n\nChangelog: An operation's Boundary group takes edge picks in any pick mode, and two separate edges now bound the area between them (touching or crossing chains are refused by name).\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1727\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
